---
import BaseLayout from '~/layouts/BaseLayout.astro'
---

<BaseLayout title="About PubID" description="Why we built PubID and where it's going.">
  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16">
    <h1 class="font-display text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight mb-6">About PubID</h1>
    <p class="text-lg text-[var(--color-text-2)] leading-relaxed mb-6">
      PubID is an open standard for universal publication identifiers — a typed, machine-readable way to identify documents across 26+ standards publishers (ISO, IEC, IEEE, NIST, and many more).
    </p>
    <p class="text-[var(--color-text-2)] leading-relaxed mb-6">
      At <a href="https://www.ribose.com" class="text-[var(--color-accent)] hover:underline">Ribose</a>, we build systems that manage standards documents — and we kept running into the same wall. Every publisher identifies documents differently. ISO uses <code class="font-mono text-sm">ISO 9001:2015</code>. IEEE writes <code class="font-mono text-sm">IEEE Std 802.3-2018</code>. NIST has <code class="font-mono text-sm">NIST SP 800-53 Rev. 5</code>.
    </p>
    <p class="text-[var(--color-text-2)] leading-relaxed mb-6">
      These identifiers carry rich semantic meaning — publisher, document type, number, year, stage, part — but that meaning is locked inside conventions that only humans can parse, and only imperfectly. PubID unlocks it.
    </p>

    <h2 class="font-display text-2xl font-semibold mt-12 mb-4">What PubID does</h2>
    <ul class="space-y-2 text-[var(--color-text-2)] mb-6">
      <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)] mt-1">→</span> <span><strong>Parse</strong> any identifier into typed components</span></li>
      <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)] mt-1">→</span> <span><strong>Render</strong> in multiple styles (full, abbreviated, short, machine-readable)</span></li>
      <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)] mt-1">→</span> <span><strong>Compare</strong> identifiers across different publishers</span></li>
      <li class="flex gap-3"><span class="text-[var(--color-accent)] mt-1">→</span> <span><strong>Map</strong> to URN for machine interchange (RFC 5141-bis compliant)</span></li>
    </ul>

    <div class="mt-12 p-6 rounded-xl bg-[var(--color-accent-soft)] border border-[var(--color-accent)]/20">
      <h3 class="font-display text-lg font-semibold mb-2">NIST: The first official adopter</h3>
      <p class="text-sm text-[var(--color-text-2)] mb-4">
        In April 2022, NIST officially published the PubID Syntax for NIST Technical Series Publications — making NIST the first standards organization to formally adopt a universal PubID scheme.
      </p>
      <a href="/publishers/nist" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1 text-sm text-[var(--color-accent)] hover:underline">
        See the NIST publisher schema <span aria-hidden="true">→</span>
      </a>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
